The HUD must associate these keys with the actual move performed by the selected fighter in the currently displayed ground or air state.

Do not display generic Attack 1, Attack 2 labels in place of the ability artwork.

Show the keyboard key itself in the tile’s bottom region.

Use compact, easy-to-read keycap styling.

The comma key must render correctly.

Support any applicable binding updates rather than permanently hard-coding the displayed labels.

9. Controller input presentation

Controller players must see their actual button bindings.

Support both PlayStation and Xbox controllers using the existing device-detection system.

Use the current fighter’s resolved controller profile, including player-customized layouts.

This is essential because Alva allows different controller mappings for different characters.

For example, character #0001’s recommended bindings include combinations such as:

