* R2 + Circle for Maximum Blue.
* L2 + Triangle for Unlimited Void.
* R2 + Triangle for Hollow Purple.

The Xbox display must use the equivalent Xbox button names.

Character #0002’s midair Bounce Attack uses a directional combination and must display that requirement clearly.

For controller bindings, support:

* Single button presses.
* Modifier + button combinations.
* Direction + button combinations.
* Hold activations.
* Different bindings for ground and air.
* Saved player remappings.

Use resolveProfile() and existing glyph/label utilities such as bindingText() where appropriate.

Do not create a second independent controller-binding table.

Input device switching

Use the existing InputManager.lastDevice behavior to determine whether to display keyboard keys or controller inputs.

When a player switches from keyboard to gamepad, the visible input labels should update accordingly.

When switching back to keyboard, restore keyboard labels.

Do not rebuild the entire HUD unnecessarily.

Do not mistake a connected but unused controller for proof that the player is actively using it.

The displayed controller button family should match the actual active controller whenever identifiable.

10. Ability ordering and readability

Arrange abilities in a consistent, logical order.

Prefer gameplay/control order or a visually sensible arrangement based on the existing controller profile.

The player should quickly understand which tile corresponds to which move.

Do not rearrange the entire ability row every time a cooldown starts or finishes.

The only major group movement should be the ground/air carousel transition.

For longer input combinations, use compact controller glyphs or a slightly wider tile instead of tiny unreadable text.

Optionally provide a discreet move-name label or accessible descriptive label for clarity.

The interface must not look cluttered.

